# Model weights and large binary artifacts, ANYWHERE in the tree.
#
# Extension-scoped rather than path-scoped, so a checkpoint written to any
# directory -- not just a run's own output -- is still caught.
#
# The asymmetry that justifies a blanket rule: weights are reproducible from a
# frozen manifest and a seed, and the record beside them is not, so the
# weights go and the record stays. A weight that genuinely must be committed
# can be forced in with `git add -f`, which is the right amount of friction
# for that decision.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.npz
*.npy
*.h5
*.pkl
*.pickle

# Large local data files, not part of the published package.
*.corpus

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# Local env (keep .env.example committed)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
